    slug: "new-testament",
    headword: "New Testament",
    category: "thing",
    body: "(Luke 22:20), rather \u201CNew Covenant,\u201D in contrast to the old covenant of works, which is superseded. \u201CThe covenant of grace is called new; it succeeds to the old broken covenant of works. It is ever fresh, flourishing, and excellent; and under the gospel it is dispensed in a more clear, spiritual, extensive, and powerful manner than of old\u201D (Brown of Haddington). Hence is derived the name given to the latter portion of the Bible. (See TESTAMENT.)",
    seeAlso: []
