    slug: "peor",
    headword: "Peor",
    category: "place",
    body: "Opening. (1.) A mountain peak (Num. 23:28) to which Balak led Balaam as a last effort to induce him to pronounce a curse upon Israel. When he looked on the tribes encamped in the acacia groves below him, he could not refrain from giving utterance to a remarkable benediction (24:1-9). Balak was more than ever enraged at Balaam, and bade him flee for his life. But before he went he gave expression to that wonderful prediction regarding the future of this mysterious people, whose \u201Cgoodly tents\u201D were spread out before him, and the coming of a \u201CStar\u201D out of Jacob and a \u201CSceptre\u201D out of Israel (24:14-17). (2.) A Moabite divinity, called also \u201CBaal-peor\u201D (Num. 25:3, 5, 18; comp. Deut. 3:29).",
