    body: "(Isa. 3:24), probably a rope, as rendered in the LXX. and Vulgate and Revised Version, or as some prefer interpreting the phrase, \u201Cgirdle and robe are torn [i.e., are \u2018a rent\u2019] by the hand of violence.\u201D",
