    slug: "sarah",
    headword: "Sarah",
    category: "person",
    body: "Princess, the wife and at the same time the half-sister of Abraham (Gen. 11:29; 20:12). This name was given to her at the time that it was announced to Abraham that she should be the mother of the promised child. Her story is from her marriage identified with that of the patriarch till the time of her death. Her death, at the age of one hundred and twenty-seven years (the only instance in Scripture where the age of a woman is recorded), was the occasion of Abraham\u2019s purchasing the cave of Machpelah as a family burying-place. In the allegory of Gal. 4:22-31 she is the type of the \u201CJerusalem which is above.\u201D She is also mentioned as Sara in Heb. 11:11 among the Old Testament worthies, who \u201Call died in faith.\u201D (See ABRAHAM.)",
    seeAlso: []
