    slug: "tale",
    headword: "Tale",
    category: "thing",
    body: "(1.) Heb. tokhen, \u201Ca task,\u201D as weighed and measured out = tally, i.e., the number told off; the full number (Ex. 5:18; see 1 Sam. 18:27; 1 Chr. 9:28). In Ezek. 45:11 rendered \u201Cmeasure.\u201D (2.) Heb. hegeh, \u201Ca thought;\u201D \u201Cmeditation\u201D (Ps. 90:9); meaning properly \u201Cas a whisper of sadness,\u201D which is soon over, or \u201Cas a thought.\u201D The LXX. and Vulgate render it \u201Cspider;\u201D the Authorized Version and Revised Version, \u201Cas a tale\u201D that is told. In Job 37:2 this word is rendered \u201Csound;\u201D Revised Version margin, \u201Cmuttering;\u201D and in Ezek. 2:10, \u201Cmourning.\u201D",
    seeAlso: []
