    slug: "zelophehad",
    headword: "Zelophehad",
    category: "place",
    body: "First-born, of the tribe of Manasseh, and of the family of Gilead; died in the wilderness. Having left no sons, his daughters, concerned lest their father\u2019s name should be \u201Cdone away from among his family,\u201D made an appeal to Moses, who, by divine direction, appointed it as \u201Ca statute of judgment\u201D in Israel that daughters should inherit their father\u2019s portion when no sons were left (Num. 27:1-11). But that the possession of Zelophehad might not pass away in the year of jubilee from the tribe to which he belonged, it was ordained by Moses that his daughters should not marry any one out of their father\u2019s tribe; and this afterwards became a general law (Num. 36).",
